# Plan a collision-free trajectory to a joint configuration (rad, joint_1..7).
# Uses native joint-space planning where the wheel supports it (exact goal),
# with an automatic FK-pose fallback; goal_mismatch_rad reports how far the
# achieved joints landed from the request — near 0 on the native path, check
# it before acting on anything that assumes exact joints on the fallback.
# Planning only — nothing moves, and this planner never touches the arm.
float64[] target_joints
# REQUIRED: the configuration the plan starts from (rad, joint_1..7).
# The caller owns the arm and its state; supplying the measured q is what
# keeps this planner decoupled from the robot. An empty or wrong-length
# vector is rejected — there is no "look at /joint_states" fallback.
float64[] start_joints
---
bool success
string message
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory trajectory
float64 planning_time
float64 goal_mismatch_rad
---
string state
